**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`

**How to implement.** A long fit runs on `JobRunner` with per-iteration progress and Cancel (001 §N 'Long fits run on `JobRunner`, with progress and cancel'; the S11.3 brief 'per-iteration progress and Cancel'; .spec-md §10.2, §10.3). The Levenberg–Marquardt solve runs whole inside one ALGLIB call (`AlglibAdapter.fs:runLm`), so the adapter, the one file allowed to name ALGLIB, reports each iteration and honours a stop request; nothing else learns of ALGLIB. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/OptimizationInterface.fs`, after `OptimizationRequest` (`OptimizationInterface.fs:OptimizationRequest`): `[<ReferenceEquality>] OptimizerIterationObserver = { reportIteration : IterationCount -> unit; cancellation : CancellationToken }`, told after each iteration of a watched solve how many it has made (1, 2, …), and read after each whether to stop (the observer shape of step 197's `KitArchiveObserver`); and `IterationWatch` = `UnwatchedIterations` | `WatchedIterations of OptimizerIterationObserver`, whether a solve is watched (a union, no flag). `TerminationReason.SearchCancelled`'s doc (`OptimizationInterface.fs:TerminationReason`) gains 'or a watched Levenberg–Marquardt solve was asked to stop (spec 0050 S11.3)', and the module doc's 'No caching, retry, or progress-callback registry lives here — progress reporting is wired separately in G.10 (slice 011).' becomes 'No caching or retry lives here; a watched solve reports its iterations through `IterationWatch` (spec 0050 S11.3).' (2) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/AlglibAdapter.fs`: `CompletionCode.terminationReason` (`AlglibAdapter.fs:CompletionCode`) gains `| CompletionCode 8 -> SearchCancelled` before its `c > 0` arm, ALGLIB's stop on a termination request; no caller requests one today, so no existing result changes. `runLm` takes `(watch : IterationWatch)`: under `UnwatchedIterations` it makes exactly today's calls (no `minlmsetxrep`, `minlmoptimize` with a null report callback), so every existing solve is bit-identical; under `WatchedIterations observer` it calls `alglib.minlmsetxrep(state, true)` and passes `minlmoptimize` an `alglib.ndimensional_rep` callback that numbers its calls k = 1, 2, …, calls `observer.reportIteration (IterationCount k)` and then, when `observer.cancellation.IsCancellationRequested`, `alglib.minlmrequesttermination(state)`; the counter is a local mutable inside `runLm`, the interop boundary. `member this.optimizeWatched (watch : IterationWatch) : Result<OptimizationResult, OptimizationError>` holds the body of `optimize ()` (`AlglibAdapter.fs:optimize`), its `LevenbergMarquardt` arm calling `this.runLm watch` and every other method running as today, unwatched (the study fit needs the LM solve only; its doc says so in one line); `optimize ()` becomes `this.optimizeWatched UnwatchedIterations`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerInverseSolver.fs`: `type IterationWatch with member this.levenbergMarquardtSolver : NonlinearSolverProxy` holds the body of `createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt ()` (`MuellerInverseSolver.fs:createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt`) with `optimizationRequest.optimizeWatched this` in place of `optimize ()`, a member because a free function of one of our types belongs on it (ELEV013); `createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt ()` becomes `UnwatchedIterations.levenbergMarquardtSolver`, its doc kept. A cancelled solve ends `OptimizationFailed`, so the proxy answers `DidNotConvergeErr` as for any failed run; the caller tells a cancel by its own token. No other member, retry or option is added. Tests, in `OptimizationInterfaceTests`: `a watched Levenberg-Marquardt solve reports each iteration and answers what the unwatched solve answers`: the AC-G1 request (r = [x0 − 3; x1 + 1] from [0; 0], `IterationCount 100`, `StepTolerance 1.0e-9`) through `optimizeWatched (WatchedIterations o)`, `o` recording each count over `CancellationToken.None`, answers the solution, iteration count and termination reason `optimize ()` answers (each coordinate within 1e-12), and the recorded counts are 1, 2, … without a gap, at least one; `a watched Levenberg-Marquardt solve stops when its cancellation is requested`: a Rosenbrock request (r = [10 · (x1 − x0²); 1 − x0] from [−1.2; 1], `IterationCount 400`, `StepTolerance 1.0e-12`, unbounded) whose observer cancels its own `CancellationTokenSource` at its first report answers `SearchCancelled` and `OptimizationFailed` after at most two reports, and the same request through `(WatchedIterations o).levenbergMarquardtSolver` as a `NonlinearRequest` with bounds ±10 answers `Error (DidNotConvergeErr _)`. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`, the cheapest class whose fits run `createAlglibLevenbergMarquardt` (step 337), shows every number unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the watch lands, a watched Levenberg–Marquardt solve MUST report each iteration and stop on a requested cancellation as `SearchCancelled`, and an unwatched solve MUST make exactly today's ALGLIB calls; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a watched Levenberg-Marquardt solve reports each iteration and answers what the unwatched solve answers` and `a watched Levenberg-Marquardt solve stops when its cancellation is requested`, the count rising by 2; unit-tests MUST pass over `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` with its numbers unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.
